    "text": "Trending Story\nUpdated 04:21 AM UTC, Thu September 25, 2025\nBlue Jays and Yankees Tied in AL East Amid Controversial Umpire Calls\nFurious baseball fans think that MLB “rigged” the Toronto Blue Jays-Boston Red Sox game on Tuesday night to help out the New York Yankees, following two controversial calls against George Springer. The Blue Jays entered Tuesday’s action with a two-game lead on the Yankees for first in the AL East, but it’s essentially a three-game … The post Furious Fans Cry Foul: MLB Rigged For Yankees After Red Sox-Blue Jays Game Rocked By Two Sketchy Game-Changing Calls [VIDEOS] originally published on Total Pro Sports .\nComments\nJC7968\nWhen we allowed gambling to be involved in our games, that changed all sports for life!\n14\nLeonard Wahl\nThe strike caught over three quarters of the plate. Should be upset he didn't swing the bat.\n6\nJust Keeping It Real\nNeither of those are clearly wrong calls although certainly questionable.\n5\nNancy Woods\nAnd yet, everyone calls Yankee fans whiners! Get over it. Tomorrow is another day.\n4\n07010401\nFoul ball, and that strike was right down the middle 🤔 But then again I am a Yankee fan 😆\n3",
